pseudo-Boolean proof version 3.0
% Positive companion to incorrect/version3/strengthening_to_core_bare_red_derived: a bare `red`
% under strengthening-to-core now stores into the core set, so the next `red` really does have
% to preserve it. Here the second witness only touches `y2`, the obligation `1 y1 >= 1` is
% discharged straight from the database, and the proof must still verify -- if the fix ever
% over-rejects, this is what breaks.
f 1;
strengthening_to_core on;
red 1 y1 >= 1 : y1 -> 1 ;
red 1 y2 >= 1 : y2 -> 1 ;
output NONE;
conclusion NONE;
end pseudo-Boolean proof;
